    "methods_description": "EEG, pupillometry, and behavioral data were collected from 32 healthy right-handed volunteers (28 included in final analysis after quality control) during a fear conditioning task. Participants performed a lateralization judgment task (left/right voice localization via keyboard response) across three phases: Pre-Conditioning (CS stimuli without US), Conditioning (CS+ paired with loud white noise US at 50% partial reinforcement; CS- unpaired), and Extinction (CS stimuli without US). Stimulus assignment (high/low amplitude modulation voices as CS+/CS-) was counterbalanced by gender across participants.",
